+---
+kind: upgrade-guide
+description: Tool callbacks replaced during a prepared execution now fail before their body runs.
+---
+
+# Tool dispatch definition identity
+
+## Change
+
+Tool calls bind the visible definition and its execution callback before policy begins. Replacing that definition or callback during `tools/pre-execute`, approval, or `tools/execute` now produces an error without invoking the replacement. Previously, dispatch could resolve and execute a different definition after the call had passed policy. Unchanged definitions and around-dispatch listeners that return their own result are unaffected.
+
+## Migration
+
+1. In plugins that replace tool registrations or mutate `execute`, finish the replacement before submitting a call through `ctx.tools.execute`.
+2. Do not use policy or around-dispatch listeners to swap the implementation of an already prepared call. Submit a new call after registration instead.
+3. Verify that the new call passes normal policy and invokes the intended definition once; an in-flight replacement must return a normal tool error.
